  "body": "A 3-axis mill can turn a workpiece when the mill spindle holds the stock and stationary lathe tools sit on the table. Today, `Family::admits` (`crates/app/src/operation/kinds.rs`) rejects turning operations on `Kind::Mill`, and `SetupDef` (`crates/app/src/schema.rs`) holds one work offset for the whole setup.\n\nAdd an optional part-in-spindle mode to `SetupDef` for `Kind::Mill` machines:\n\n- Store the stock length-offset register `H` (for example `255` for `G43 H255`).\n- Store the collet nose stick-out and outer diameter.\n- Store a list of table tool stations. Each station maps one lathe tool to a unique 1-based work offset index (`WorkOffset`), an approach side (`-X` or `+X` in the first slice), and a spindle direction (`M3` or `M4`).\n- Add undoable commands and MCP tools (`crates/app/src/commands/`, `crates/app/src/mcp/`) to configure the mode and stations.\n- Save and load the new fields in the project file (`crates/app/src/project/`).\n- Admit `Family::Turn` operations and on-centre `Drill` operations in a part-in-spindle setup.\n- Refuse milling operations in a part-in-spindle setup.\n- Refuse two active tools that share one work offset index.\n- Require `SetupDef::workholding_max_rpm` (`crates/app/src/setup_workholding.rs`) in a part-in-spindle setup, and enforce that RPM limit on `Kind::Mill` when this mode is active.\n\nDone means: undoable commands and MCP tools configure part-in-spindle mode and table stations on a `Kind::Mill` setup, project save and load preserve them, turning operations generate and simulate in `crates/app/src/stock_sim_lathe.rs`, milling operations and duplicate station offsets are refused by name, and an unset `workholding_max_rpm` blocks posting.\n\nPart of #2580\n",
